    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0345" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/1670</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5682</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-26">June 26, 1933</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        1.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Legation’s previous
                    reports, particularly to despatch No. 5666 of June 20, 1933,<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d210-f1"/> regarding the plans of the Colombian National Government
                    for payment of interest on its external funded debt, I have the honor to report
                    that the original plan (the Legation’s despatch No, 5646 of June 9, 1933<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d210-f2"/>) to have one-third of the interest due during the
                    current year paid in cash and two-thirds in non-interest-bearing scrip,
                    amortizable on October 1, 1937, or any prior date at the option of the
                    Government, will be followed. The possible modifications in the plan outlined in
                    the first paragraph of the Legation’s despatch No. 5668 of June 21, 1933, seem
                    to have been abandoned without serious consideration.</p>
                <p>It is understood that an announcement of the Government’s offer was made in New
                    York yesterday.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d210-f3"/> It is further understood that
                    the offer covers not only the 35 million and 25 million dollar loans of the
                    Colombian Government floated in the United States but also the loans of the
                    Agricultural Mortgage Bank guaranteed by the Government.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Allan Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d210-f1" n="41" xml:id="d210-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d210-f2" n="41" xml:id="d210-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d210-f3" n="42" xml:id="d210-f3-content">
                <p>The contract was signed in New York on June 30, 1933, renewing the loan to
                    September 30, 1933. A further contract was signed at the end of September
                    renewing the loan to December 31, 1933. (821.51/1692, 1719)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
